;  The 24 fps measured on 2026-09-07 was K = 86,000 - that gap is what the decal line cost.
;  (The SP 57 -> 32 measurement implies K = 104,000 and disagrees by ~7%. 97,000 is the
;  conservative fit and it is the one confirmed twice at SP 60.)
;  With decals back at stock and shadow maps back at 2048, SP 60 should land near 27-29, plus
;  whatever turning vsync off gives back (at 60 Hz it was quantising frames to 30 or 20).
;  THIS TABLE IS THE ONLY WAY TO TARGET A SPECIFIC FPS. Every other line in this file is a
;  guess; this one has measured points behind it. To go past ~30, spend SP - nothing else
;  in the file has anywhere near that much left in it.
;
;   1  r.ScreenPercentage        60 -> 70 -> 80. Still the best looks-per-frame buy;
